# Architecture

**Today:** Jira list → hunt PDFs → eye-match → type log → write email → maybe update Jira.

**Target:** Pull Jira → scan job-folder PDFs → score matches → review board → fill `TRANSMITTAL` on the existing CT/ST/FT Excel books (macros stay) → File Transmittal in Excel or DocCon File + PDF → confirm send → Outlook + Jira writeback + folder copy.

## Trigger (Sarah runs DocCon)

Engineer emails Sarah the list and details. No new Jira status or include-field. Sarah opens DocCon, enters Job Number, console **fetches every Jira issue with that Job Number** (plus children of the job Project), she selects this pack and can **edit the fields on the board**. Confirm **writes Jira**. Outlook from the DocCon mailbox is a later confirm. After Load the navy bar shows the Jira **Project** name (blue) and the Dropbox job folder (teal) so she can confirm she is on the right job.

## Match engine

Find the Dropbox **job root** under `2.1 Current Jobs` (also `2.0` / completed). Job Number is the Jira grouping key; the folder may be a shared parent (`2026-049-1` and `2026-049-2` in `2026-049`). Hunt: folder whose name **is** the typed Job Number (or `Job Number …` title), then a parent-job folder; if several still match, do not pick — **Locate job folder…**. A this-PC mapping (LOCALAPPDATA) remembers the pick. Name mismatch is expected. Scan `2.0 Drafting/**/Current PDF/*.pdf`. Also scan `1.0 Engineering` (MR), `4.0 Quality/4.3` (ITP & WO), `4.7` (weld summary), and job-local `4.4.1` if it exists. Weld procedures also come from the shared person-folder `4.4 QC / 4.4.1 WPS&PQR` (`EIS-1 (Rev 4).pdf`); unmatched library PDFs are not extras. Skip Void / VOIDS / Old Procedures. Filename `{id} REV {rev}.pdf` (`ITP-…`, `WO-…`, `MR-…`, `WS-…`) or `EIS-n (Rev x).pdf`. Paste PDF, Assign, Locate…, and the watched folder stamp Next Outgoing Rev from that token (yellow when it differs from Jira Now; no REV leaves Next alone; Load hunt does not dirty every matched row; Confirm still writes Jira). Jira `2026-075-1-STWD` matches PDF `2026-075-STWD`. High / Missing on the board. Missing: operator **Locate…** the file, or **Paste PDF** (Outlook Copy of one or more attachments, then the navy button or Ctrl+V). A single paste pairs the selected row; several wait in **New PDFs** for Assign one by one (copied into {job}/3.0 Doc Con/DocCon/dropped/, then paired; Explorer original stays; not filed into Current PDF). Re-paste of the same Outlook filename overwrites our leftover inbox and `dropped/` copy; numbered `-2` names are only for two files in the same paste that share a name. When Outlook FileContents is empty, the paste child pastes the clipboard IDataObject into the inbox the same way Explorer pastes into a folder. There is no floating Drop PDFs overlay and no teal dock. There is no **PDF from Outlook** hunt button — Copy in Outlook then Paste PDF (or the watched folder) is the ingest. Clipboard read stays in a one-shot child (python -m doccon.drop_host --paste). The watched folder (Downloads / Desktop / inbox) is the fallback. A paste pair shows the PDF **filename** then **— email dropped** on the PDF address (yellow bypass), so the operator can confirm which file paired; the filename leads because the PDF column is narrow, and hover carries the full wording plus the staged path. Hunt or Locate… to a real job/Current PDF outside `DocCon/dropped` restores the plain filename, clears the yellow, and **deletes our `dropped/` copy**. Confirm success deletes dropped copies used on packed rows; abort does not. **Open** beside Locate opens the paired PDF in the Windows default reader (disabled until a file is paired; missing file is a short error). OCR later. Never auto-send.

## Three panes (workstation)

1. Register — job Drawing Package; each row shows **last record** and the operator **edits** JIRA ID, Description, Status, Client Doc No., Outgoing Rev, Submitted to Client For, Submission Date, Return Request Date, Incoming Rev, Client Approval Status, Return Date, Shop/Field IFC rev and dates, and EDDI Status **on the console**. Status, Submitted to Client For, Client Approval Status, Shop/Field IFC Rev, and EDDI Status are pick-only lists. Jira Due Date is not an operator field; Confirm copies a newly entered Return Request Date onto `duedate`. Cover **Expected return** stamps packed Next Return Request Date to the same calendar day. Cover **Date issued** stamps packed Next Submission Date the same way. Load starts **Date issued** at today and **Expected return** at N/A with Pack off. Pack-tick with blank/N/A does not wipe a typed Next; setting a cover date back to N/A restores that packed Next date to Now. Cancel Next restores every Next to Now, Date issued to today, and Expected return to N/A. The drawing list scrolls sideways. Confirm writes Jira (not a live keystroke). Mail is a later confirm.
2. Match board — Jira row vs PDF vs confidence
3. Preview — title block and previous transmittal

Cover (FROM / TO / CC / project) is a **bottom strip**, not a side column, so the drawing list keeps full width.

## Transmittal log (Excel, not a new file)

Job folder `3.0 Doc Con`:

- Client: `3.1 Client Transmittals/3.1.1 Out/CT-{job}.xlsm` + `CT-{job}-{n}.pdf`. Incoming returns: `3.1.2 In/{date} …`
- Shop: `3.2 Shop Transmittals/ST-{job}.xlsm` + `ST-{job}-{n}.pdf`, then copy IFC/ITP/MID/BOM
- Field: `3.3 Field Transmittals/FT-{job}.xlsm` + `FT-{job}-{n}.pdf`, then copy into `8.0 Field Construction Folder/2.0 IFC Drawings & Transmittals` (no MID/BOM)

`TRANSMITTAL` is the next send. Numbered sheets `1`, `2`, … are history. The original `.xlsm` stays the log: **Add Page** and **File Transmittal** must still work by hand. DocCon **Confirm…** writes Jira Next values, fills the working sheet, copies a numbered tab, prints the cover PDF, prints a dated EDDI snapshot of listed items that have a paired PDF (`EDDI-{job}-{date}.xlsm` / `.pdf` in `3.0 Doc Con`; copy of the live `EDDI-{job}.xlsm` sheet **Project**, groups 1–9 from Next values; printed group titles merged A:M and centered with orange fill kept; empty 1–9 groups hidden; stranded page breaks in hidden regions dropped; Missing / no-file rows stay on the console; not only packed drawings; live book unchanged; skip Generic and ungrouped; not attached to Outlook). **EDDI…** prints that snapshot without filing a transmittal. Then it attaches that transmittal PDF and a zip of the drawing PDFs (the form is not in the zip) in Outlook, and opens a draft (one click; operator clicks Send). Unused filed tab keeps the number (`FILED IN ERROR, NOT USED YET`).

## PEP (`7.0 Sales`)

Project Execution Plan is the job card for the cover. Form is sheet `C-109.5` (Excel, printed to PDF). Pick the highest Rev whose name is this Job Number — not a leftover from another job.

- **TO** = emails already on the CT/ST/FT TRANSMITTAL sheet when filled; otherwise Transmittal Recipients Main (`D50`) from the PEP — default only; editable on the console. Addresses only.
- **CC** = emails already on the letter when filled; otherwise Transmittal Recipients CC (`D51`) plus any emails in the PEP PM/PE cells — default only; editable on the console. Addresses only; add more with a semicolon. Names and roles are not shown.
- Cover project line uses the letter’s PROJECT DESCRIPTION when filled; otherwise Client, site LSD, tank tag, PO, WO/MOC from the PEP — default only; editable on the console
- **Locate PEP…** overwrites TO / CC / project from that PEP
- Shop/Field cover **TO / CC** are not the PEP client recipients. They come from that ST/FT letter if Sarah already filled them; otherwise they stay empty. Confirm does not require TO for ST/FT.
- FROM stays `doc.control@eliteintegrityservices.com` (not an operator edit)
- Date issued and Expected document return are console fields (Date issued = today on Load; Expected return = N/A until a calendar pick or **Urgent same day** / **Urgent +1** / **7 days** / **14 days**). Expected return stamps packed Next Return Request Date to that calendar day; Date issued stamps packed Next Submission Date the same way (Client / Shop / Field share the same widgets). Pack-tick with blank / N/A does not wipe those row dates. Setting a cover date back to N/A restores that packed Next date to Now. Changing either cover date to a real day re-stamps currently packed rows. Cancel Next restores every Next to Now, Date issued to today, and Expected return to N/A.
- Pack draft is saved as `{job}/3.0 Doc Con/DocCon/client-pack.json` (Dropbox). It holds cover TO/CC/project, Locate… / dropped PDF paths (`email_dropped` bypass metadata), and dirty Next edits (keyed by Jira issue key). Auto-save before Load of another job and on quit; Next edits debounce (~1s). Load restores Next / PDFs / TO/CC/project, then still unpacks, sets Date issued to today and Expected return to N/A (Save may write ticks/dates; Load ignores them). Machine settings stay in LOCALAPPDATA, including saved TO/CC addresses. Do not write console edits back into the Sales PEP.
- On Load, more than one EDDI Status on an issue prompts for a single group 1–9; Update writes that option to Jira and reloads. Skip continues Load without changing Jira. Generic (0) stays off the board.
- If Sales has no usable PEP, the operator locates the file (Excel C-109.5 preferred; PDF if that is all they have)
- Real job: highest Rev whose filename is this Job Number. Sandbox `2026-Tanzim` has no PEP of its own; a copied PEP in `7.0 Sales` is the test stand-in. Blank C-109.5 and leftover template PEP PDFs are not auto-picked.

Mail: **Confirm…** uses `doc.control@eliteintegrityservices.com` when that Outlook account is on this PC; otherwise the signed-in default (Chris, Tanzim, Sarah). Never auto-send. Attaches `CT|ST|FT-{job}-{n}.pdf` and `{cover_id}.zip` of the drawing PDFs (the transmittal form is not in the zip). Operator clicks Send in Outlook. Cover FROM on the Excel sheet stays `doc.control@…`. Shop/Field still copy into IFC folders later (no MID/BOM on Field).

## Build slices (do not start until asked)

1. Match + log (fill TRANSMITTAL; File still works in Excel; optional DocCon File + PDF; email and Jira update still manual)
2. Outlook send + client zip in `3.1.1 Out` + Jira writeback + shop/field folder copy
3. Delta vs last pack, per-client templates, multi-job queue

Skip a client portal unless a client demands it.

